CON-05: send a covered barrel's rain to LID runoff when it cannot be returned

lid_getRunoff() adds the rain falling on a covered rain barrel to the flow
returned to the pervious area, but subcatch_getRunon() only applies that
flow when the subcatchment has a pervious non-LID area. On a 100 %
impervious subcatchment, or one filled by LIDs, the rain was dropped from
the water balance. In that case add it to the LID group's surface runoff,
which leaves through the subcatchment outlet.

Requires: CON-04

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-05_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
index 395ac7a..1fa17bb 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
@@ -1701,8 +1701,13 @@ void lid_getRunoff(int j, double tStep)
             if (lidProc->lidType == RAIN_BARREL &&
                 lidProc->storage.covered == TRUE)
             {
-                // Add runoff from closed rain barrel to return (cfs)
-                qReturn += subcatch->rainfall * lidArea;
+                // Add runoff from closed rain barrel to return (cfs),
+                // or to LID surface runoff if there is no pervious area
+                // to return it to (see subcatch_getRunon)
+                if (subcatch->area > subcatch->lidArea &&
+                    subcatch->fracImperv < 1.0)
+                    qReturn += subcatch->rainfall * lidArea;
+                else qRunoff += subcatch->rainfall * lidArea;
 			}
             else
             {
